claim.claim-text:
providing an upstream USB port for communication with a USB host;
providing a downstream USB port for communicating with a consumer USB device;
receiving USB signals from the consumer USB device via the downstream USB port;
routing the USB signals emanating from the consumer USB device to the upstream USB port via a USB bridge and a USB hub in accordance with a determination that the consumer device is operating in a USB host mode; and
routing the USB signals emanating from the consumer USB device to the upstream USB port via the USB hub and bypassing the USB bridge in accordance with a determination that the consumer device is operating in a USB device mode.

receiving first USB host signals from a first USB host;
receiving second USB signals from a consumer USB device;
determining whether the second USB signals emanating from the consumer USB device indicate whether the consumer USB device is acting as a second USB host; and
routing the second USB signals emanating from the consumer USB device while acting as the second USB host to the first USB host via a USB bridge and a USB hub.

receiving a first USB host signal from a first USB host;
receiving a second USB signal from a consumer USB device;
determining whether the second USB signal emanates from a second USB host;
establishing a first communication path via a USB bridge and a USB hub between the first USB host and the consumer USB device in accordance with the second signal emanating from the second USB host; and
establishing a second communication path via the USB hub between the first USB host and the consumer USB device thereby bypassing the USB bridge in accordance with the second USB signal not emanating from the second USB host.
